1.1 Functional Requirements (FRs)
Req. ID	Requirement	Type	Priority	Verification Method
FR-01	The robot shall accept a delivery request only when it is in IDLE state.	FR	High	Functional test
FR-02	The robot shall start navigation after accepting a valid delivery request.	FR	High	State-transition test
FR-03	The robot shall detect obstacles and suspend navigation when an obstacle is detected.	FR	Critical	Simulation test
FR-04	The robot shall resume navigation after confirming that the obstacle has been avoided.	FR	High	Functional test
FR-05	The robot shall deliver the medicine package only after reaching the destination.	FR	Critical	State-transition test
FR-06	The robot shall return to the warehouse after delivery.	FR	High	Functional test
FR-07	The robot shall abandon delivery and return to the warehouse when the battery reaches the emergency level.	FR	Critical	Battery simulation
FR-08	The chamber shall monitor temperature, humidity, vibration, door status, and power.	FR	Critical	Sensor integration test
FR-09	The system shall authenticate the operator and check their role before accepting a robot command.	FR	Critical	Security test
FR-10	The system shall record robot commands, status reports, and significant safety events in an event log.	FR	High	Log inspection
1.2 Non-Functional Requirements (NFRs)
These measurable targets are proposed for the pilot system because the scenario does not specify exact performance limits. They should be approved by the project team.
Req. ID	Requirement	Type	Priority	Verification Method
NFR-01	The system shall enter Safe Mode within 3 seconds of detecting a critical battery or chamber-temperature condition.	NFR	Critical	Timed test
NFR-02	The system shall support at least 20 robots connected simultaneously.	NFR	High	Load test
NFR-03	The system shall reject every robot command from an unauthenticated or unauthorised operator.	NFR	Critical	Security test
NFR-04	The system shall display a received robot status update within 5 seconds after the update reaches Mission Control.	NFR	High	Performance test
NFR-05	The portal shall allow an authorised user to find a robot or operator record within 3 seconds under normal pilot load.	NFR	Medium	Usability/performance test
1.3 High-Risk Requirements
Req. ID	Requirement	Type	Priority	Verification Method
SAFE-01	The robot shall enter Safe Mode within 3 seconds when a critical battery or chamber-temperature threshold is crossed.	Safety	Critical	Fault-injection and timing test
SAFE-02	The robot shall never enter a railway crossing unless the barrier is open and no train is approaching.	Safety	Critical	Crossing simulation
SAFE-03	The robot shall stop or enter an appropriate safe condition if the control link is lost during a safety-critical activity.	Safety	Critical	Communication-loss test
SAFE-04	The robot shall not deliver medicine while handling an obstacle or while the chamber door is open.	Safety	Critical	State and sensor tests
